BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vermont History Trivia at Brookfield Old Town Hall
DTSTART:20260910T190000
DTEND:20260910T210000
DTSTAMP:20260910T150255Z
UID:a965576e195bd2081d7b6b608fe5d2@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Brookfield Old Town Hall for a special event brough
 t to you by our friends at the Vermont Historical Society. Vermont History
  Trivia is a great way to have fun with friends and family. Expertise isn
 ’t necessarily needed- questions are multiple choice to help newbies and
  history lovers of all ages engage with our state’s past (and present). 
 For 2026\, VHS has created special sets of questions that explore aspects 
 related to the 250th anniversary of the U.S. within Vermont. You may learn
  about things like early Vermonters\, significant battles\, Indigenous cul
 ture\, or Vermont place names. Come as a team or as an individual and we w
 ill team you up with others from the community. Sponsor: Eastrise Credit U
 nion\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Brookfield Old Town Hall\, 93 Stone Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/vermont-hi
 story-trivia-at-brookfield-old-town-hall-18-08-2026-12-53-03
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Visiting Writer Reading: Shelley Wong
DTSTART:20260910T200000
DTEND:20260910T210000
DTSTAMP:20260910T150255Z
UID:551595eaa19004eb7257438b57a1db@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Shelley Wong is the author of As She Appears (YesYes Books\, 2
 022)\, longlisted for the National Book Award for poetry and winner of the
  Lambda Literary Award for lesbian poetry and the Pamet River Prize. She l
 ives in San Francisco. Wong has taught creative writing at the University 
 of San Francisco MFA program and the Ohio State University and led worksho
 ps for Kenyon College\, Arizona State University\, Poets & Writers\, and M
 innesota State University at Mankato. Born and raised in Long Beach\, Cali
 fornia\, she is queer and fourth-generation Chinese American. She holds an
  MFA in creative writing from the Ohio State University and a BA in Englis
 h from UC Berkeley. The 2026 Visiting Writers Program is generously suppor
 ted by The Rona Jaffe Foundation. VSC is pleased to partner with independe
 nt bookseller\, Phoenix Books.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Studio Center\, 80 Pearl Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/visiting-w
 riter-reading-shelley-wong-01-09-2026-13-19-01
END:VEVENT
