BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Intro to Ethnic Hand Percussion Workshop
DTSTART:20260912T100000
DTEND:20260912T113000
DTSTAMP:20260910T150255Z
UID:b8878e213ff29ab67a51f9f9ef71ef@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating 30 years of ethnic hand percussion\, Drum Journeys
  of Earth welcomes all members of the community to visit the studio to att
 end a FREE introductory workshop in ethnic drumming and percussion\, inclu
 ding West African djembe\, Afro-Latin conga\, Middle Eastern doumbec\, Nat
 ive American medicine drum\, and pow-wow drumming. Date: Saturday\, Septem
 ber 12th\, 2026 Location: Drum Journeys of Earth Building 5 of the Howe Ce
 nter Rutland\, VT Drum Journeys of Earth and its students are widely known
  for leading the Rutland Halloween Parade as the Drumming Skeletons. Stude
 nts have also performed at First Night\, at the Northern New York NAACP Fu
 ndraising dinner\, with Soul Bath Trance Dance\, and the Twice Baked Orche
 stra. As a Broadway actor and founder/director of Drum Journeys of Earth (
 DJE)\, Gary Meitrott brings his theatrical talents to drum circles\, perfo
 rmances\, and workshops\, in addition to his weekly classes. His vibration
 s reach out to the community\, creating a ripple that touches all ages –
  inviting them to come and play with the drum. Rhythm is a universal langu
 age that allows us to connect with our inner selves and with community. It
  has a meditative quality that calms our minds and reduces anxiety. Drummi
 ng also boosts activity in the brain’s neural pathways\, leading to “b
 rain plasticity\,” enhanced memory\, and other cognitive skills. Researc
 h shows that group drumming improves concentration\, reduces stress\, alle
 viates pain\, and boosts the immune system. What’s more\, the mental and
  physical engagement is exhilarating\, making it ideal for young and old a
 like. There is a multi-sensory engagement involving visual\, auditory\, an
 d tactile senses. For more information or to join Beginning classes\, plea
 se call 802-282-2581\, email Gary_Meitrott@comcast.net\, or log on to http
 s://garymeitrottunlimited.org/. 0.00\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Drum Journeys of Earth\, Bldg 5 of the Howe Center 1 Scale Avenue
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/free-intro
 -to-ethnic-hand-percussion-workshop-28-07-2026-19-42-27
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lake Champlain Challenge Race 2026
DTSTART:20260912T090000
DTEND:20260912T140000
DTSTAMP:20260910T150255Z
UID:d9b3ad5c955afe67055587d5152462@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The Lake Champlain Challenge Race is a community race at Lake 
 Champlain Maritime Museum open to all human-powered boats with a post-run 
 lunch for all! Bring your own boat\, experience the beauty of Lake Champla
 in from a new angle\, and enjoy a day of community-fueled fun and competit
 ion. Individual and team participants all set off on a fun three-mile cour
 se past the palisades\, one of the most picturesque parts of Lake Champlai
 n\, racing to set the fastest time per category. The only requirement is p
 articipating boats must be propelled by human power\, nothing else! Race c
 ategories include: Coxed rowing gigs (six and four oared)\, fixed and slid
 ing seat single rowers\, double rowboats\, kayaks\, canoes\, paddleboards
 \, and miscellaneous watercraft. After the race\, all are invited to enjoy
  a free lunch buffet\, hosted by the Museum’s rowing clubs\, and a fun a
 ward ceremony. Advance online registration for the Challenge Race is stron
 gly encouraged to guarantee your spot in the race and to ensure we have en
 ough food for everyone for lunch.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Lake Champlain Maritime Museum\, 4472 Basin Harbor Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/lake-champ
 lain-challenge-race-2026-17-06-2026-16-29-22
END:VEVENT
